WEBVTT

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:04.382
Advanced SQL is mostly about controlling intermediate results and row context.

00:00:04.382 --> 00:00:07.777
A CTE gives a meaningful name to a stage in the query.

00:00:07.777 --> 00:00:12.662
A window function lets one row see related rows without automatically collapsing the result.

00:00:12.662 --> 00:00:15.422
Sequence functions depend on a meaningful order.

00:00:15.422 --> 00:00:18.467
And throughout the module, grain still matters.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:23.157
At every stage, you should be able to complete the sentence: one row represents what?

00:00:23.157 --> 00:00:27.282
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:27.282 --> 00:00:32.537
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:34.687
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:40.207
In a real setting such as a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region,

00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:45.542
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:45.542 --> 00:00:46.897
before discussing syntax.

00:00:46.897 --> 00:00:52.160
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
